      "message": "Without this patch, we are actually double accounting the RT utilization when WALT is in use.\n\nWhat I don\u0027t like is just that we add yet another WALT/PELT conditional block.\n\nPerhaps we can fix this and get the change to clean up a bit the current FAIR+RT aggregation by using the compilation guards we already have in place.\n\nWhat about doing the aggregation in cpu_util_freq(), only when required (i.e. !WALT or WALT is disabled)?\n\nThat way:\n - boosted_cpu_util() will remains WALT/PELT agnostic\n - we avoid to explicitly collect RT contributions from sugov_get_util(),\n   which are ultimately not required when WALT is in use\n\nHere it is a possible alternative path:\n   https://pastebin.com/XNgzUWKs\nimplementing this idea.\n\nThoughts?",
